# **the tail is where a pointer stops meaning the pointer**, and the IR is what says so. with the
# deref back, `[$text]` reads the byte at `$text[0]` - 65 - and hands `%s` an address of `0x41`. the
# `OUT` above does catch that, unlike the promotion story next door: no platform prints `AB` from a
# byte reinterpreted as a pointer. what the IR adds is *where* it went wrong, so a regression reads as
# "the pointee is being loaded again" rather than as a crash inside libc

--- OUT --->
<AB|AB>
<hi|AB>
--- IR --->
# the declaration is still variadic, the tail parameter being no parameter at all in LLVM. first
# because a positive CHECK advances a cursor and the declarations come out above the definitions
CHECK: declare i32 @snprintf(ptr, i64, ptr, ...)
CHECK: define i32 @main(

# nothing between the entry and the call reads *through* either pointer. the bytes of "AB" are
# written with `store i8`, and a `load i8` in this window is the auto-deref coming back - which is
# the whole regression, stated without naming an SSA number that a later change would renumber
CHECK-NOT: load i8
CHECK: @snprintf(ptr
